target: internal/record/parity_test.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestSaysNoSuchRunReadsBothSignals'
expect: FAIL: TestSaysNoSuchRunReadsBothSignals
why:    comparing the WHOLE stderr buffer against "unknown" is the third wrong version of this guard and the one a reviewer is most likely to restore, because it reads as stricter. It is not stricter, it is brittle: any interpreter warning at import makes a HEALTHY oracle fail the gate, which is the exact sensitivity that separating stderr from stdout was introduced to remove. No fixture puts noise on stderr, so this entry and its test are the only things that can see the regression.
--- old
	return lastLine(stderr) == "unknown"
--- new
	return strings.TrimSpace(stderr) == "unknown"
